Spike: Define Similarity Score Approach for Comp Search




Key details
Description

Description

P0 requires the platform to rank comparable records using a similarity indexation / relevance score.

This spike is to define how the similarity score should work across P0-supported property types ( All of the current Property types )  and comp types. The spike should cover how the score is calculated, how it is stored, and how it is presented to appraisers.

The goal is not to implement production scoring logic yet, but to define the approach and identify the open questions that need PVA/appraiser validation.

Relevant P0 Requirements: 

FR27.1
FR27.2.1
FR27.2.2
FR28.GAP4

Scope

Review the latest P0 requirements related to comp search, suggested comps, ranking, relevance score, and similarity indexation.

Define the recommended approach for calculating the similarity score.

Identify candidate scoring inputs, such as proximity, submarket, property type, size, recency, quality/class, amenities, data completeness, and prior usage.

Identify which fields should be used to filter results versus rank results.

Document if certain property types or comp types need specific scoring inputs.

Define how the score should be stored, including whether to store composite score, score breakdown, scoring version, selected comp score, and user overrides.

Define how the score should be presented to appraisers, such as a single relevance score, score breakdown, reason codes, sorting, or ranking explanation.

Expected Output

Recommended similarity scoring approach

Candidate scoring inputs

Filtering vs ranking fields

Property-type or comp-type specific considerations

How the score is calculated

How the score is stored for audit/debugging

How the score is displayed to users

Open questions for PVA/appraiser validation

Acceptance Criteria

P0 similarity/ranking requirements are reviewed.

Candidate scoring inputs are documented.

Filtering vs ranking fields are identified.

Initial calculation approach is recommended.

Storage/audit approach is documented.

UI presentation approach is documented.

Property-type and comp-type specific considerations are documented.

Open questions for PVA validation are documented.

POC

Show an example of how the final similarity score results would display to the user (Does not need to include programatic calculations).